From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:27:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] docs: say when to turn on
 terminal.update_survivable_processes

---
 website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
index 9b48a23a4d..c72f3e651b 100644
--- a/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
+++ b/website/docs/user-guide/configuration.md
@@ -398,6 +398,9 @@ processes outlive a gateway or backend restart (for example a Hermes update):
 
 Without a usable scope the setting logs one warning and nothing changes.
 
+A host that applies Hermes updates without first waiting for running work to finish should turn this on:
+the update then interrupts a turn, not the long command the turn was running.
+
 ### Docker Backend
 
 Runs commands inside a Docker container with security hardening (all capabilities dropped, no privilege escalation, PID limits).
